Unfortunately this is a real bug.  It will be fixed for 3.1, of course, but
you may have to wait a while.

In artifact.c is a function get_artifact().  It checks if (otmp).  This should
be if (otmp && otmp->onamelth).  When a name is "erased", the name length
is set to zero, but the data in the name is not itself changed.  Since this
function forgot to check the length, it would still consider an artifact
with an erased name as having a name, despite the name being invisible to the
player.

Note this is, of necessity, an _unofficial_ fix.
